2. Original source of the questions: BAMF
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The underlying questions, answers and illustrations are those of the official
test catalogue published by the German Federal Office for Migration and Refugees
(Bundesamt für Migration und Flüchtlinge, BAMF):

    Gesamtfragenkatalog zum Test "Leben in Deutschland" / Einbürgerungstest
    Bundesamt für Migration und Flüchtlinge (BAMF)
    https://www.bamf.de/SharedDocs/Anlagen/DE/Integration/Einbuergerung/gesamtfragenkatalog-lebenindeutschland.pdf

This attribution is given as the source citation that redistribution of an
official German work requires (§ 5 (2) UrhG, source-attribution duty). It is not
a claim that BAMF endorses, reviewed, or is involved with this app — see
section 6.

`scripts/verify-questions.ts` checks the shipped text against that catalogue and
writes `src/data/verification-report.json`. Where the shipped wording departs
from the catalogue, every departure is deliberate, individually justified in
`scripts/build-questions.ts`, and listed in README.md under "Data quality".

The 43 images in `public/img/` are illustrations belonging to those catalogue
questions. They reached this repository through the dataset in section 1, which
referenced them on a third-party host (`foreignvasi.com`); they are mirrored here
so the app works offline and does not depend on a host that will eventually rot.
No `foreignvasi.com` reference remains anywhere in the build output — the build
fails if one does.

No per-state coat of arms is shipped. `src/data/states.ts` carries a `wappen`
field pointing at the exam's own composite illustration, and the state picker
deliberately renders an ISO code instead, precisely because separately licensed
emblem assets are not part of this dataset.


