4. Runtime and build dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

npm dependencies are not vendored into this repository. Their licenses are those
declared in their own packages and resolved in `package-lock.json`; run
`npm ls --all` or inspect `node_modules/<pkg>/LICENSE` for any individual one.

The only third-party code that reaches the browser at runtime beyond the app
bundle is the Firebase JS SDK (Apache-2.0), loaded lazily and only when sync is
both configured and used.


5. What this app sends anywhere
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Recorded here because provenance runs both directions. With sync unconfigured or
signed out, nothing leaves the device: no analytics, no ads, no telemetry, no
third-party requests, no CDN. When a user signs in to the optional Firebase sync,
their own progress document is stored in that project's Firestore under their own
uid, readable and writable only by them (`firestore.rules`). Fonts, images,
questions and translations are all self-hosted.


